cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal,
  work-in-progress synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI
  assistant by Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed,
  and not a new result.
title: "academic-writing-and-presentations (work in progress)"
abstract: >-
  How to write research papers, mathematical articles and proofs, and how
  to build presentations, so that they are cheap to read or to follow. An
  extension of reader-ergonomics: the evidence and document shapes
  particular to these genres.
  Use it as a reading list and a starting point, not as an authority.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/academic-writing-and-presentations"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - research papers
  - mathematical writing
  - proofs
  - presentations
  - literature review
